    "question": "There are 3 boxes of cereal. One box holds 14 ounces of cereal. Another box holds half the amount of the first box and 5 ounces less than the third box. How much cereal is there in all 3 cereal boxes?",
    "gold": "33",
    "answer": "First = <<14=14>>14 oz\nSecond = (1/2) * 14 = <<(1/2)*14=7>>7 oz\nThird = 7 + 5 = <<7+5=12>>12 oz\n14 + 7 + 12 = <<14+7+12=33>>33 oz\nThere are 33 ounces of cereal in those 3 boxes.\n#### 33"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total amount of cereal in all three boxes, we need to find the amount of cereal in each box and then sum these amounts.\n\n1. The first box holds 14 ounces of cereal.\n2. The second box holds half the amount of the first box. Therefore, the amount of cereal in the second box is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{14}{2} = 7 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n3. The second box also holds 5 ounces less than the third box. Let the amount of cereal in the third box be \\( x \\) ounces. Then we have:\n   \\[\n   7 = x - 5\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( x \\), we get:\n   \\[\n   x = 7 + 5 = 12 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n   So, the third box holds 12 ounces of cereal.\n\nNow, we sum the amounts of cereal in all three boxes:\n\\[\n14 + 7 + 12 = 33 \\text{ ounces}\n\\]\n\nThus, the total amount of cereal in all three boxes is \\(\\boxed{33}\\).",
